# CO rottemp/vibtemp corrected 2026-10-26 (were O2's 4.14 K / 2256 K). Source: Horton, JPL TR 32-1425 (1970), Sec. II.d,
#   CO X1Sigma+ constants from Krupenie, NSRDS-NBS 5 (1966); also Huber & Herzberg (1979) / NIST WebBook:
#   we = 2169.8 cm^-1 -> vibtemp = hc we/k = 3122 K (harmonic, as in the code's SHO partition function);
#   Be = 1.931, alpha_e = 0.0175 cm^-1 -> B0 = 1.922 cm^-1 -> rottemp = 2.77 K; symmetry number 1 (heteronuclear).
#   VibRel (5.58659E-5) is still O2's placeholder; unused with relax variable vibmodel MW (vibrel() overrides it).
CO  28.01    4.65E-26  2    0.2  2.77   2    5.58659E-5    3122.0    1.0      0.0
